# Rock edges (#547): the room end walls are natural rock, not built pillars. Three variants per side (`rock-r-*`: air on the right, the
# moon-lit face with a light rim; `rock-l-*`: air on the left, a dark ramp) and a foot each where the wall meets the floor. They reuse the
# unused sheet ids 1-3, 5-7 and 9-10 (gids 2-4, 6-8, 10-11). The outer edge wobbles up to 3 px inward inside the 16 px collision column (it
# never passes it); the top and bottom rows of every variant are plain, so any variant stacks on any other, and the inner columns are plain, so
# the two columns of a room join meet with no seam. `retile` picks the variant by place and puts them only in the first and last column of a room.
